      "content": "Leucine, a key branched-chain amino acid, acts as a signaling molecule that kicks off muscle protein synthesis. It's a crucial activator of the mechanistic Target of Rapamycin, or mTOR complex 1 (mTORC1). When leucine is present, it binds to specific receptors or interacts with other cellular components, which then leads to the activation of mTORC1. This activation is the master switch that tells the cell, \"Time to start building muscle!\" and initiates the cascade of processes required for hypertrophy.",
